  "worked_solution": "The ratio of the amount of cotton fabric to the amount of linen fabric is $5:4.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nThis means that there are $\\frac{5}{4}$ meters of cotton fabric for each meter of linen fabric.",
